WEBVTT

00:11.200 --> 00:14.403
<i>Gathered together from the cosmic reaches of the universe.</i>

00:14.539 --> 00:16.212
<i>Here in this great hall of justice</i>

00:16.235 --> 00:20.590
<i>are the most powerful
forces of good ever assembled.</i>

00:25.754 --> 00:26.978
<i>Superman,</i>

00:31.092 --> 00:32.569
<i>Batman and Robin,</i>

00:35.984 --> 00:37.692
<i>Wonder Woman,</i>

00:41.399 --> 00:43.130
<i>Aquaman,</i>

00:45.423 --> 00:46.565
<i>and Meg.</i>

00:47.078 --> 00:53.929
<i>Dedicated to truth,
justice and peace for all mankind.</i>

01:01.211 --> 01:02.648
Hey, Quagmire,
what've you got there?

01:02.671 --> 01:05.396
<i>It's the new Sports Illustrated
Swimsuit Issue. Check it out.</i>

01:05.516 --> 01:07.759
Those swimsuit issues don't
excite me like they used to.

01:07.880 --> 01:10.050
I've been spoiled by internet porn.

01:10.051 --> 01:11.276
- It's true.
- Totally.

01:11.277 --> 01:13.143
What do you mean internet porn?

01:13.144 --> 01:15.490
You uhh... don't know about internet porn?

01:15.551 --> 01:17.541
Don't know what?
I'm not really a computer guy.

01:17.542 --> 01:19.648
Quagmire, I would think you,
of all people,

01:19.660 --> 01:21.541
would know about internet porn.

01:21.661 --> 01:25.591
They got like thousands, literally
millions of naked pictures on the internet.

01:26.408 --> 01:27.094
What?

01:27.095 --> 01:29.088
And videos! Thousands of them!

01:29.227 --> 01:30.353
You guys are messing with me.

01:30.354 --> 01:31.922
Quagmire, you don't use the Internet?

01:31.923 --> 01:34.316
You mean that crappy dial-up thing?
It's a pain in the ass!

01:34.317 --> 01:36.565
No I don't use the damn internet!
I thought that was for nerds!

01:36.685 --> 01:37.730
Why didn't you guys tell me!

01:37.850 --> 01:41.170
Oh yeah, you can even see Tonya Harding's honeymoon video on there.

01:41.171 --> 01:45.427
I mean... It's gross,
but it's like famous gross.

01:45.428 --> 01:48.933
You know, these women don't compare to
the old swimsuit issues with Kathy Ireland.

01:48.934 --> 01:50.767
Yeah she had it going on!

01:50.834 --> 01:53.952
You know, Horace still has one of those old
beer promotional cutouts of her from like

01:53.987 --> 01:57.016
1994, in the backroom.
Don't you, Horace?

01:57.017 --> 01:59.406
Hey, you mean this thing?
I was about to throw it out.

01:59.526 --> 02:01.372
If anyone wants it, it's theirs.

02:07.073 --> 02:18.503
в™Є Suddenly,
life has new meaning to me. в™Є

02:18.504 --> 02:26.424
в™Є There's beauty up above and
things we never take notice of. в™Є

02:26.425 --> 02:34.246
в™Є You wake up and suddenly
you're in love. в™Є

02:37.024 --> 02:39.079
I'm taking you home with me.

02:45.184 --> 02:47.943
Hey Dad.
Where you going with that cutout?

02:47.944 --> 02:49.944
Hey kids, this is Kathy.

02:49.945 --> 02:52.214
We're designing lifestyle products together.

02:52.215 --> 02:54.512
It's completely legitimate,
but don't tell your mother.

02:59.036 --> 03:01.437
I had a great time today at the museum.

03:01.438 --> 03:03.555
You were the most beautiful woman there.

03:03.556 --> 03:07.598
You know... Lois won't be home
from groceries for a while.

03:07.718 --> 03:09.352
I have an idea.

03:14.597 --> 03:16.641
Knock knock, anyone in the bathroom?

03:25.601 --> 03:28.329
I love the time we spend together,
you know that?

03:28.643 --> 03:30.400
Hey Kathy, guess what?

03:30.631 --> 03:35.470
I'm out... under the table,
right now... I'm out.

03:35.802 --> 03:37.202
- Peter!
- Oh no.

03:37.203 --> 03:41.393
What the hell is going on?
I sent you to pick up dinner an hour ago!

03:41.394 --> 03:43.400
What are you doing with that cutout?

03:43.651 --> 03:45.703
You know what, Lois,
I'm glad you found out!

03:45.704 --> 03:48.016
I can't carry on this charade anymore!

03:48.051 --> 03:49.616
I have an announcement to make.

03:49.820 --> 03:51.166
No no, I'll do it, I'll do it.

03:51.167 --> 03:54.277
I know I been able to keep this a secret.
But Kathy and I

03:54.278 --> 03:57.141
are not actually working on
a project together.

03:57.458 --> 03:59.613
We're... in love!

04:00.400 --> 04:01.396
You're an idiot.

04:01.397 --> 04:02.984
My lawyer will call your lawyer.

04:03.246 --> 04:05.352
Ugh, this is stupidest thing
he's done since he got

04:05.353 --> 04:07.493
in that turf war with that cat.

04:15.344 --> 04:16.408
Hey shut up!

04:20.810 --> 04:23.460
Now kids, you don't have to
call her Mom right away,

04:23.495 --> 04:25.610
but I do want you guys to get along.

04:25.746 --> 04:27.622
Just give her a chance,
I think you'll like it.

04:27.623 --> 04:30.523
Maybe she'll let us do things
that Lois won't let us do.

04:30.578 --> 04:33.843
Yeah! Hey Mom,
can I pull my pants down?

04:34.746 --> 04:36.705
If she doesn't answer,
does that mean yes?

04:36.706 --> 04:37.768
That's what I been going with.

04:37.791 --> 04:40.829
Yay! Ha ha ha ha
ha ha ha ha ha...

04:40.950 --> 04:43.171
- I want to get in on that!
- Ha ha ha ha ha ha...

04:44.748 --> 04:47.126
Mine's better, mine's better, mine's better!

04:50.531 --> 04:52.070
Oh, hello Lois...

04:52.190 --> 04:54.521
I would've thought you would've
moved in with your mother by now.

04:54.556 --> 04:57.321
No Peter, I'm just pretty much letting this run its course.

04:57.322 --> 05:00.397
Well I'm sorry you're handling this so poorly,
but have you seen Kathy?

05:00.398 --> 05:02.048
We were gonna go get our passports renewed.

05:02.049 --> 05:04.623
Uh Chris took her into his room
about ten minutes ago.

05:04.624 --> 05:06.764
What? That whore!

05:06.765 --> 05:10.319
She's betrayed me worse than
Lady Macbeth betrayed Duncan!

05:16.605 --> 05:19.880
I uhh...
I don't know Shakespeare very well.

05:20.209 --> 05:23.223
Kathy? Kathy!

05:23.691 --> 05:27.700
There you are! Oh, don't give me that look.
You don't think I know where you been?

05:27.701 --> 05:29.980
How dare you make a fool of me!

05:29.981 --> 05:33.625
Did you have sex with that fat kid?
Did you? Answer me!

05:33.968 --> 05:36.349
Oh my God,
look what you made me do!

05:39.483 --> 05:43.213
Why did you have to provoke me?
Why did you hav...

05:43.671 --> 05:46.555
Quagmire? Hey uh...
Nobody's seen you in days!

05:46.745 --> 05:47.778
Hey, Peter.

05:48.523 --> 05:52.787
I just been uhh... checking out
some of that internet porn.

05:52.910 --> 05:53.804
You okay?

05:53.805 --> 05:56.233
Yeah yeah I'm good I'm good I'm good...
I'm just gonna...

05:56.760 --> 05:58.908
Go... go and check my mail over there.

05:59.093 --> 06:00.247
You been lifting weights?

06:00.248 --> 06:05.394
Uhh no... no...
I don't think uhh... No.

06:06.963 --> 06:09.884
I'm... I'm sorry Peter, I gotta...
I gotta get back.

06:15.755 --> 06:18.191
I'm sorry, Lois,
I was a fool!

06:18.192 --> 06:20.627
I'm done with Kathy!
Can you ever forgive me?

06:21.896 --> 06:24.548
Peter, settle down.
Yes I forgive you,

06:24.571 --> 06:27.066
just as long as you are done
with that stupid cutout.

06:27.081 --> 06:29.392
I just want you to know that
every time I was with her,

06:29.513 --> 06:30.947
I was thinking of you.

06:32.738 --> 06:36.231
Peter, stop.
Come on, I'm not in the mood.

06:39.310 --> 06:40.827
Oh, Peter!

06:40.948 --> 06:45.608
Oh, Lois, I've missed you! You and your
wonderful smile and your beautiful eyes

06:45.609 --> 06:48.214
and your awesome third boob
that's on top of the other boob.

06:48.215 --> 06:53.147
What? Oh my God!
Peter, that's not a boob, that's a lump!

06:53.148 --> 06:54.741
A lump? Holy crap!

06:57.427 --> 07:01.743
Peter, stop that! We're not having sex!
I just told you I have a lump!

07:01.744 --> 07:04.204
I got a lump too and mine is easier to get rid of.

07:08.172 --> 07:11.911
Mrs. Griffin, I've got good news.
Your test results came back negative

07:12.005 --> 07:15.567
It appears the lump in your breast is not
"black gross boob death."

07:15.568 --> 07:16.484
Breast cancer?

07:16.485 --> 07:18.044
That's the layman's term, yes.

07:18.372 --> 07:19.612
Oh, thank God.

07:19.733 --> 07:22.026
- What a relief!
- Yeah, that was scary.

07:22.131 --> 07:24.463
Now Mrs. Griffin, although you are
in the clear for the moment,

07:24.486 --> 07:26.452
we need to have a look at
your family medical history

07:26.464 --> 07:28.265
to determine your future risk.

07:29.458 --> 07:33.085
Huh, that's curious. I didn't realize your
mother was a Holocaust survivor.

07:33.086 --> 07:37.328
My mother? Oh no that's...
That's impossible, she's not Jewish.

07:37.388 --> 07:39.757
According to her birth certificate, she is.

07:39.800 --> 07:41.703
Oh my God!

07:41.704 --> 07:45.080
Wow, breast cancer's starting
to look pretty good.

07:49.878 --> 07:51.759
Mom, you're Jewish?

07:51.760 --> 07:54.320
I'm sorry I never told you, dear.

07:54.321 --> 07:57.056
When we were married,
tour father made me conceal the fact

07:57.057 --> 07:59.586
so he could get into country clubs.

07:59.587 --> 08:03.282
- It was the right thing to do.
- It was the right thing to do, dear.

08:03.468 --> 08:04.500
Oh my God!

08:04.501 --> 08:07.335
So Granda Hebrewberg
is actually Jewish?

08:07.336 --> 08:11.316
Yes, when she moved to America,
her family changed their name.

08:11.317 --> 08:14.421
It was originally
Hebrewberg-Moneygrabber.

08:14.422 --> 08:17.915
That makes you Jewish, Lois,
and your children too.

08:17.916 --> 08:19.300
Well, this kinda rocks my world.

08:19.530 --> 08:21.963
Even more than the time
when I went to that pediatrician.

08:22.851 --> 08:26.453
Woah, Stewie,
you're getting to be a big boy.

08:26.454 --> 08:28.866
I think somebody is gonna be a football star.

08:28.928 --> 08:30.683
Oh, you...

08:30.684 --> 08:32.408
Oops, forgot your chart,
be right back.

08:33.472 --> 08:37.138
Woah, Jason,
you're getting to be a big boy.

08:37.139 --> 08:39.895
I think somebody is gonna be a football star.

08:40.085 --> 08:42.150
I can't believe I fell for that line.

08:42.151 --> 08:45.147
I actually let myself believe I could
be a doctor's wife.

08:45.335 --> 08:48.088
You're just fat, Stewie,
silly and fat.

08:51.707 --> 08:53.554
Thanks you for coming over, Max.

08:53.555 --> 08:56.701
I really need some advice from
an actual Jewish person.

08:56.702 --> 08:58.148
Oh, it's my pleasure, Lois.

08:58.149 --> 09:00.601
I'm sure this all must be
very overwhelming.

09:00.602 --> 09:03.109
I just don't know what to
do with this information.

09:03.110 --> 09:05.677
I spent my whole life as a Christian.

09:05.678 --> 09:08.152
I'll tell you what you should do with it,
absolutely nothing!

09:08.153 --> 09:09.393
That's the problem with this world.

09:09.394 --> 09:11.540
Too many people go overboard
with what they believe.

09:11.773 --> 09:14.702
Like Quagmire, when he thought
he was the one getting the spin-off.

09:14.874 --> 09:16.392
See you later, bitches.

09:16.393 --> 09:20.405
Have fun with your stupid (bleep)
giant chicken jokes and your Conway Twitty.

09:20.406 --> 09:22.643
Hey, why is there a moving truck
outside Cleveland's house?

09:22.820 --> 09:26.418
Well, I wouldn't put it quite like that,
but essentially Brian's right.

09:26.419 --> 09:30.137
Being Jewish doesn't really have to
change you or your family's life.

09:30.138 --> 09:31.620
Wow, I guess you're right.

09:31.621 --> 09:34.282
There's no reason things should
be any different around here.

09:34.441 --> 09:36.418
Shalom, Jews!

09:36.419 --> 09:39.954
Wow dad, where did you get all
that glistening chest hair?

09:39.955 --> 09:41.508
Came with my Star of David.

09:41.509 --> 09:42.773
Peter, what is all this?

09:42.774 --> 09:46.378
Look, this is my way of letting you know
that I'm embracing who you are.

09:46.393 --> 09:48.036
Oh, and I don't respond to Peter.

09:48.037 --> 09:49.965
From now on
I want you to use my Hebrew name.

09:53.100 --> 09:55.200
Well, I... I caution you uhh...

09:57.318 --> 10:00.413
that becoming Jewish
doesn't happen overnight.

10:00.414 --> 10:04.644
It's a process that involves
spiritual education and good works.

10:04.645 --> 10:06.916
So what you're saying is that it happens overnight?

10:06.917 --> 10:09.140
Look, Peter, I am the one
with the Jewish heritage,

10:09.141 --> 10:11.554
and I really don't want to make
a big deal out of this.

10:11.555 --> 10:14.387
Leave it to a Jew to take all
the fun outta being a Jew.

10:14.388 --> 10:17.825
Now listen up, I like the hat and I
like the scarf, so we are doing this.

10:21.735 --> 10:25.030
Kids, from now on,
this is where we will celebrate the Sabbath.

10:25.031 --> 10:27.044
Peter, this is all unnecessary.

10:27.062 --> 10:29.145
Our life was fine the way it was.

10:29.162 --> 10:31.132
Check it out!
I'm one of you guys now, huh.

10:31.133 --> 10:35.004
I'm Jewish, yeah!
Holocaust! We're number one!

10:35.034 --> 10:37.416
Look at all these short, hairy men.

10:37.464 --> 10:40.110
God I feel like I'm on the forest moon of Endor.

10:40.533 --> 10:41.806
Good afternoon.

10:41.807 --> 10:44.201
As we approach the Passover holiday,

10:44.202 --> 10:46.582
let us remember the struggle of our people

10:46.583 --> 10:50.542
as they labored under the yoke
of Pharaoh's despotic rule.

10:50.543 --> 10:53.256
Hey, if anyone appreciates
a good yoke it's the Yews.

10:56.137 --> 10:58.486
That's my Jewish laugh.
I'm working on a Jewish laugh.

10:58.487 --> 11:00.676
Peter, I am so embarrassed right now.

11:00.677 --> 11:02.247
Can we please just go?

11:02.517 --> 11:05.692
- Hi, you're pretty.
- Oh, thank you.

11:07.258 --> 11:10.436
Mom, is sodomy illegal
if you're Jewish?

11:10.437 --> 11:13.074
I hope to so, Meg. I really do.

11:13.781 --> 11:16.747
It's not, Lois.
It's not.

11:20.384 --> 11:22.829
Dad, this isn't the
way to school.

11:22.830 --> 11:24.098
Yes it is, Chris.

11:24.099 --> 11:25.897
One of the best parts about being Jewish

11:25.898 --> 11:28.420
is getting to take advantage
of their excellent schools.

11:28.421 --> 11:30.191
I'm not going to no Jewish school.

11:30.192 --> 11:33.107
Sitting around all day
with a bunch of short, hairy guys,

11:33.108 --> 11:35.600
I feel like I'm on the forest moon of Endor.

11:35.649 --> 11:38.446
Didn't you... didn't you make
that joke the other day?

11:38.447 --> 11:42.370
Oh... yeah... No I was...
I wasn't sure that everybody had umm...

11:43.500 --> 11:45.404
had heard.

11:47.696 --> 11:49.835
And instead of lasting for one day,

11:49.836 --> 11:52.614
the oil in the lamp lasted for eight days,

11:52.615 --> 11:54.989
and this is why we celebrate Hanukkah.

11:54.990 --> 11:56.384
Yeah yeah yeah, how long before we play

11:56.385 --> 11:58.864
"Pin the eviction notice
on the black guy's door."

11:58.865 --> 12:00.615
Now does anyone have any questions?

12:00.616 --> 12:03.153
Yeah I have a question. What are you
gonna do when Jesus comes back

12:03.154 --> 12:04.657
and puts a boot up your ass?

12:04.658 --> 12:09.027
And it's also why many families
give their children eight days of presents.

12:09.251 --> 12:11.562
Wait, did she say eight days of presents?

12:11.563 --> 12:12.236
Yeah.

12:12.237 --> 12:14.930
Well, this Judaism thing is
gonna be better than I thought.

12:14.931 --> 12:17.173
Alright class,
that's all for today's lesson.

12:17.174 --> 12:18.847
Now everyone off to gym class.

12:19.350 --> 12:21.511
Alright, today we're gonna play soccer.

12:29.553 --> 12:30.722
Huh, that was easy.

12:34.718 --> 12:37.224
Hey Lois, the kids are all asleep

12:37.225 --> 12:39.228
I suppose they are

12:39.822 --> 12:44.429
You know what else? I picked out a sexy
little Jewish outfit for you at the store

12:44.430 --> 12:45.614
What is that?

12:45.615 --> 12:49.486
Oh my God Lois, if you put on this long,
thick dress right now I will lose it.

12:49.487 --> 12:51.374
Peter, I'm not wearing that thing.

12:51.469 --> 12:53.035
And if you put this
shawl over your head ...

12:53.156 --> 12:55.910
Ooh, you have clunky,
unfashionable, peasant shoes?

12:56.031 --> 12:58.767
Oh, I swear to God, Lois.
I swear to God that I would lose it.

12:58.787 --> 13:00.672
Peter, get off me!

13:01.182 --> 13:03.789
Tell me I don't earn as much
as your friend's husband!

13:04.158 --> 13:06.680
Peter, stop it!
I'm going to sleep.

13:06.972 --> 13:09.070
Fine, I'll just sit here and watch TV.

13:09.649 --> 13:14.106
<i>We now return to Mark Wahlberg
in "Annoyed and Confused."</i>

13:14.528 --> 13:16.700
What? What's going on?

13:16.735 --> 13:19.252
I don't get it.
Man, I gotta work out.

13:19.287 --> 13:23.210
What's going on here?
Where am I? What the... huh?

13:23.340 --> 13:26.578
What the hell is going on here?
Huh? What?

13:32.875 --> 13:34.331
Peter!

13:38.092 --> 13:39.081
Dad?

13:39.116 --> 13:40.961
What do you think you're doing, Peter?

13:40.996 --> 13:42.822
You were raised Catholic.

13:42.857 --> 13:47.140
If you rescind your religion,
you will spend eternity... in hell!

13:47.175 --> 13:48.875
Oh God, I don't want that!

13:48.910 --> 13:51.549
Then you better not fall
for all the Jewish stuff.

13:51.605 --> 13:54.262
Oh... alright,
if that's what you think is best.

13:55.736 --> 13:57.694
Oh wait, Dad,
before you to go, can you say:

13:57.814 --> 14:00.108
"Peter, you must go to the Degobah System"?

14:00.499 --> 14:04.441
Peter, you must go
to the Degobah System.

14:05.761 --> 14:06.649
Thanks.

14:10.529 --> 14:12.847
Anybody want toast or a bagel?

14:14.737 --> 14:16.096
Peter, what the hell!

14:16.097 --> 14:18.553
Lois, last night my father came to me

14:18.589 --> 14:20.193
and reminded me
that I am a good Catholic.

14:20.194 --> 14:23.734
If I don't rid the house of this Jewish curse,
this family is gonna go to hell!

14:23.735 --> 14:25.195
And I won't let that happen!

14:25.196 --> 14:28.686
Peter, you were the only one who was even
taking this thing seriously.

14:28.722 --> 14:29.915
Jews are gross, Lois.

14:29.916 --> 14:31.858
It's the only religion with the word 'ew' in it.

14:31.859 --> 14:34.280
Oh, come on. You're acting
crazier than when you were

14:34.304 --> 14:36.226
going through your Parker Lewis phase.

14:36.347 --> 14:38.058
Peter, you ready for dinner?

14:38.092 --> 14:39.981
Ah, that's just like the Parker Lewis episode

14:40.016 --> 14:41.407
when Parker Lewis ate dinner.

14:41.408 --> 14:43.883
Peter, nobody cares about your canceled show.

14:43.884 --> 14:48.160
Lois, Parker Lewis can't lose.
Don't even try and make him lose,

14:48.195 --> 14:50.570
because it's just gonna be
that much more embarrassing for you

14:50.606 --> 14:52.808
when you realize that he can't lose.

14:52.843 --> 14:54.506
Would he win in a fight with Batman?

14:54.507 --> 14:56.532
Well, Chris, think about what you're saying.

14:56.567 --> 14:58.318
Parker Lewis can't lose.

14:58.319 --> 15:00.880
Heretofore, Batman can suck on that.

15:00.922 --> 15:05.804
Suck on that? Suck on this!
TicTacs only have 1.5 calories!

15:05.839 --> 15:06.716
Well played.

15:06.717 --> 15:08.143
I love you, Dad.

15:08.144 --> 15:10.285
I love you too, son.

15:20.081 --> 15:22.169
What the... what the hell!

15:22.170 --> 15:24.746
How do you like it? Huh?
How do you like it?

15:24.781 --> 15:26.532
Peter, what in God's name is this?

15:26.533 --> 15:29.384
Wait a minute,
are these pieces of Stewie's crib?

15:29.762 --> 15:31.547
I hate it here!

15:34.962 --> 15:37.135
Well, thanks for spending time
with me today, Mom.

15:37.136 --> 15:40.890
I just had to get out of that house,
Peter is being such a jackass.

15:40.891 --> 15:44.144
Lois, I think this more serious than you realize.

15:44.145 --> 15:45.658
Don't you see what he's doing?

15:45.659 --> 15:47.536
Oh, he's just being immature.

15:47.536 --> 15:49.514
It's happened before and it will pass.

15:49.515 --> 15:51.808
Lois, what Peter is doing to you is

15:51.809 --> 15:54.525
exactly what Carter did to me for years.

15:54.560 --> 15:57.810
He's repressing your Jewish identity!

15:58.544 --> 16:01.534
But Mom, I don't really care
about being Jewish,

16:01.558 --> 16:03.926
or even Christian for that matter!

16:03.961 --> 16:06.725
I just want to be
a good person on my own.

16:07.569 --> 16:09.754
All I'm saying is I let your father take

16:09.789 --> 16:13.994
my Jewish identity and I've
regretted it ever since.

16:14.029 --> 16:16.995
I don't want to see you
make the same mistake.

16:17.030 --> 16:20.206
I don't know, Mom.
I'll think about it.

16:20.241 --> 16:21.324
Carter, knock it off!

16:21.660 --> 16:24.332
Come on, you know you Jew girls want that dollar!

16:24.367 --> 16:26.275
Follow the dollar and it'll lead you to...

16:26.620 --> 16:30.003
What... what does Jews like?
Salmon! There's salmon over here!

16:30.234 --> 16:31.703
Is there really salmon over there?

16:31.704 --> 16:35.141
No, you walk over there and
he squirts you with a squirt gun.

16:51.751 --> 16:53.455
What the hell!

17:00.947 --> 17:02.861
Are you out of your (bleep) mind?

17:02.862 --> 17:06.653
Relax, Lois, I was aiming for the mailbox,
I'm just trying to make point

17:06.654 --> 17:07.847
Good morning, Lois

17:08.736 --> 17:11.437
Peter, for God sake!
I am so sorry, Mort.

17:11.438 --> 17:14.409
No problem, Lois.
That's just how people say hello to me.

17:15.259 --> 17:16.470
- Hey, Joe.
- Hey, Mort.

17:19.674 --> 17:22.126
Peter, you and I are
gonna have a conversation.

17:22.127 --> 17:24.844
- I am very angry with you.
- Geez, what's your problem?

17:24.845 --> 17:28.286
What you did this morning was
so far outta line, I just...

17:28.287 --> 17:30.655
Let me tell you this,
Mom was right.

17:30.903 --> 17:34.197
I can't just sit here and let you
dump all over my heritage.

17:34.198 --> 17:36.498
I'm not gonna make the mistake she did.

17:36.533 --> 17:38.677
I'm Jewish and I am proud of it.

17:38.678 --> 17:41.260
And this weekend
we're having a Passover Seder.

17:41.261 --> 17:43.867
- You can't do that, it's Easter!
- Not in this house.

17:43.868 --> 17:46.259
Lois, this family believes
in the Easter Bunny.

17:46.260 --> 17:48.884
He died for our sins
in that helicopter crash.

17:48.885 --> 17:50.812
Now, if you want to go hell, that's fine.

17:50.813 --> 17:54.763
But don't drag the rest of us down with you
like a mentally handicapped rooster.

17:58.611 --> 18:00.419
Good night, everybody!

18:04.037 --> 18:05.542
Okay everyone,

18:05.642 --> 18:07.725
this is my first time doing a Seder,

18:07.726 --> 18:11.653
which is where we tell the story of the
Jews' escape from bondage in Egypt.

18:11.654 --> 18:14.234
Doesn't it seem like every Jewish holiday

18:14.235 --> 18:16.239
has to do with them escaping from stuff?

18:16.240 --> 18:17.376
No, Chris.

18:17.377 --> 18:21.277
And you know, tricking some bigger, more athletic people...

18:21.278 --> 18:22.868
Uhh... Lois, not that I'm rushing you,

18:22.869 --> 18:24.364
but when do we get to the wine drinking?

18:24.365 --> 18:26.450
Hang on! Hang on!
Before do anything,

18:26.451 --> 18:28.612
I'd like to say a blessing over
the candles, if I may.

18:28.968 --> 18:31.394
Now bear with me,
I haven't had much rehearsal time.

18:44.122 --> 18:45.133
Can't we just eat?

18:46.294 --> 18:48.056
And now I shall continue with the prayer

18:58.697 --> 19:01.365
And now let's move on to
the washing of the hands.

19:01.400 --> 19:03.599
This is a very important part
of the cerem...

19:03.619 --> 19:06.326
Hey, hey, hey!
The Easter Bunny is here!

19:06.327 --> 19:07.961
Happy Easter!

19:07.962 --> 19:10.451
Peter, what the hell are you doing in that...

19:10.452 --> 19:11.467
Have you been drinking?

19:11.502 --> 19:13.047
Not since I got out of the car.

19:13.048 --> 19:15.348
Who here thinks I can
kick my ass?

19:15.349 --> 19:18.390
Peter, you are not gonna ruin this
Seder. Now get outta here.

19:18.425 --> 19:19.998
I'm sorry, kids.

19:19.999 --> 19:22.981
I just wanted to help
Brian run for mayor.

19:23.373 --> 19:26.104
I guess I forgot
what was really important.

19:26.116 --> 19:27.580
Peter, just go lie down.

19:27.701 --> 19:31.288
Alright, I'm gonna go lie down, and then I'm
gonna come back and mess up your Seder.

19:32.133 --> 19:34.822
Alright, I'm back and
I'm much more sober.

19:34.823 --> 19:36.105
Lois, what you're doing is wrong.

19:36.106 --> 19:38.292
I want you to get all this
Jew food off the table.

19:38.293 --> 19:39.900
I most certainly will not!

19:39.901 --> 19:41.736
It's me or your religion, Lois.

19:41.737 --> 19:44.303
I am a Catholic and I want
to live in a Catholic house.

19:44.304 --> 19:46.895
Well, I'm a Jew and I want
live in a nicer house.

19:46.896 --> 19:48.558
Do you really think
I should run for mayor?

19:48.559 --> 19:51.672
Peter, you have got to stop
living in your own stupid world!

19:51.673 --> 19:55.028
I'm sorry, but I can't be with someone who doesn't believe in Jesus.

19:55.191 --> 19:57.303
Hey hey, heard my name!

19:57.338 --> 19:58.498
Wow, Jesus!

19:58.499 --> 20:00.895
Oh, you're dead now, Lois.
Jesus is gonna kill ya.

20:00.896 --> 20:03.484
And then we gonna bury you in the
yard, next to Kathy Ireland...

20:04.490 --> 20:06.163
Er, I mean uhh...
Nice weather we're having!

20:06.364 --> 20:09.833
Look Peter, I thought it might
interest you to know that I'm Jewish.

20:10.215 --> 20:10.913
What?

20:10.948 --> 20:12.580
He's Jewish, Peter.

20:12.615 --> 20:15.469
Jewish, like full on,
like you practice Jewey-ism?

20:15.470 --> 20:16.328
I am a Jew.

20:16.329 --> 20:19.125
Prove it! What's a 9% tip
on a $200 bill?

20:19.126 --> 20:21.567
$18, which is fair...

20:21.568 --> 20:23.420
Oh my God, it's true!

20:23.579 --> 20:24.956
But I'm so confused.

20:24.957 --> 20:26.502
Peter, it really doesn't matter.

20:26.503 --> 20:29.267
Catholicism and Judaism
are not that different.

20:29.268 --> 20:30.883
They're two sides of same coin.

20:31.144 --> 20:33.928
In fact, the Last Supper, one of
the most iconic images of the

20:33.929 --> 20:36.558
Catholic faith, was a Passover Seder.

20:36.559 --> 20:39.947
And if I'm not mistaken, Islam
is also in that same spiritual family.

20:39.948 --> 20:41.841
Uhh... Let's not muddy things up here.

20:41.842 --> 20:44.803
The most important thing
is to treat other people

20:44.838 --> 20:46.879
the same way you would
want to be treated.

20:46.880 --> 20:48.979
Ooooh... an eye for an eye!

20:49.251 --> 20:52.164
Well, Lois,
I guess I owe you an apology.

20:52.401 --> 20:55.639
I was scared because my dad
convinced me I was going to hell.

20:55.640 --> 20:58.814
And I was doing it to make up
for my mother's mistake.

20:58.815 --> 21:02.522
Look, I don't know if being Jewish is
the right thing for our family.

21:02.757 --> 21:06.327
I just wanted the chance to explore it
so I could know for sure.

21:06.462 --> 21:09.310
But to tell you the truth,
I thought we were fine before.

21:09.511 --> 21:12.633
But, then Jesus,
which religion should our family be?

21:12.634 --> 21:14.384
Six to one, they are all complete crap.

21:14.385 --> 21:15.388
Thank you!

21:15.389 --> 22:16.389
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru